    "lawCode": "Amd §§222 & 203, rpld §221, Eld L",
    "lawSection": "Elder Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S502\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the elder law, in relation to the senior citizen energy\npackaging pilot program and making technical changes thereto; and to\nrepeal section 221 of such law relating to the legislative intent\nunderlying the senior citizen energy packaging pilot program\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo make technical amendments to certain sections of the elder law.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1.  Amends section 222 of the\nElder Law.  Makes technical corrections by moving the legislative\nintent for the senior citizen energy packaging pilot program from\nsection 221, where it was separated from the program, into section\n222 where the program is established.\n\nSection 2.  Repeals section 221 of the Elder law.\n\nSection 3.  Amends section 203, subdivision 8 of the Elder Law.\nRenumbers subdivision 8 to subdivision 9.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nThis bill makes technical corrections to current law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nIt is important to have clarity within the law to avoid\nmisunderstanding and confusion. These technical corrections will help\nmaintain that clarity within the Elder Law.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2010: S.8323 - Referred to Rules/A.11304 - Passed Assembly\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
